<title>USA: CCF Holding withdraws its stock buyback.</title>
<headline>CCF Holding withdraws its stock buyback.</headline>
<dateline>JONESBORO, Ga. 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>CCF Holding Co, the holding company of Heritage Bank, said it withdrew the request it placed with the U.S. Office of Thrift Supervision for the repurchase of five percent of its common stock.</p>
<p>The company said the OTS indicated that in view of previous stock repurchases it would not approve the company's request to buy up to 41,215 shares that was announced June 12, 1997, CCF Holding said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The bank holding company needs approval of stock repurchases made within three years of a mutual-to-stock conversion of a bank.</p>
</text>
